WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:07.236
First, real compilers break any single descriptive law, so this study defines a seven-part yardstick instead.

2
00:00:07.576 --> 00:00:15.189
Second, maximum compiler optimization burns upfront energy that never pays back on thirty percent of test programs.

3
00:00:15.529 --> 00:00:23.674
Third, fingerprinting code by variable position reuses builds with zero mix-ups, cutting Rust compile energy four hundredfold.
